### Fix B2: rename condition
**File:** `SaveAndContinueService`, in `processAgendaResponse`, inside the guidedPermission branch that runs when `nextQid` is blank.

```java
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// RENAME Special1/2/3 → real section names when guided permission ends.
//
// WHY THIS CHANGED:
//   Before, the rename ran ONLY when the saved question was in
//   specialEndsAt (5A, 31A). With back navigation, a user can finish the
//   journey by changing an EARLIER question (e.g. 1A → EMI only).
//   The journey was complete, tasks.json said COMPLETED / Check Your
//   Answers, but the rename never ran because 1A is not in specialEndsAt.
//   Result: Special1/Special2 rows stayed in DB and the task list broke.
//
// HOW IT WORKS NOW (two ways to rename):
//   1. specialEndsAt.contains(questionId)
//        → today's rule, kept exactly as is, so the normal forward
//          journey (ending at 5A or 31A) behaves the same as before.
//   2. isGuidedPermissionJourneyComplete(...)
//        → NEW. Covers finishing from any other question (1A–4C) after
//          going back. Only checked when there are no validation errors.
//
// WHY checkSpecialNameByFirmId > 0 IS FIRST:
//   Once guided permission is finished the Special rows are gone (count 0),
//   so the extra DB call in the helper never runs for task list sections.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if (firmDataItemExtDao.checkSpecialNameByFirmId(firmDataItemId) > 0
        && (specialEndsAt.contains(questionId)
            || (!hasAnyBusinessErrors
                && isGuidedPermissionJourneyComplete(firmDataItemId, merged, dataProcessingInfo)))) {
    restService.updateSpecialSections(String.valueOf(firmDataItemId));
}
```

### New helper method
**File:** `SaveAndContinueService`. Put it next to `isQuestionAnswered()`.

```java
/**
 * Checks whether the guided permission journey is really finished, so the
 * Special1/2/3 rows can be renamed even when the last save was NOT 5A or 31A
 * (e.g. the user went back and changed 1A).
 *
 * WHY WE DON'T CHECK SPECIAL1 QUESTIONS (1A–4C) HERE:
 *   This method is only called when nextQid is blank. For a guided permission
 *   save, nextQid comes from findNextUnansweredQuestion, which already:
 *     - checks every Special1 question that applies (using the dependency map)
 *     - always includes 5A
 *     - includes 31A when Section 10 applies
 *   So a blank nextQid already means Special1 has nothing pending.
 *   Checking 1A–4C again here is NOT safe: hidden questions (e.g. 4C when
 *   4B = named firm) are sometimes in neither COMP_QUES_ID nor
 *   SKIPPED_QUES_ID, which would block the rename by mistake.
 *
 * WHAT WE DO CHECK (extra safety for the cross-section part of the journey):
 *   - 5A is answered or skipped
 *   - 31A is answered or skipped, OR Section 10 does not apply
 *
 * @return true  → safe to rename the Special rows
 *         false → do not rename (same as today's behaviour)
 */
private boolean isGuidedPermissionJourneyComplete(
        Long firmDataItemId,
        SaveREP027DataItemRequest merged,
        DataProcessingInfo dataProcessingInfo) {

    // One DB read (HTTP call to DIMS) for all rows of this firm data item.
    // We don't use isQuestionAnswered() because it makes a new HTTP call
    // every time it is called.
    List<FirmDataItemExt> journey =
            restService.retrieveFormJourney(firmDataItemId, dataProcessingInfo);

    // RestService.retrieveFormJourney returns null when the DIMS call fails.
    // In that case don't rename — this is the same as today's behaviour,
    // so a DIMS problem can never make things worse than now.
    if (journey == null) {
        LOGGER.warn("[isGuidedPermissionJourneyComplete] journey null → no rename "
                + "firmDataItemId={}", firmDataItemId);
        return false;
    }

    // "Done" = answered (COMP_QUES_ID) OR skipped (SKIPPED_QUES_ID) in any row.
    // Same rule findNextUnansweredQuestion uses, so both stay in agreement.
    Set<String> done = new HashSet<>(completedQuestionIdsFromDb(journey));
    done.addAll(skipQuestionIdsFromDb(journey));

    // 5A is always part of guided permission (findNextUnansweredQuestion
    // always adds it), so it must be done before we rename.
    boolean fiveADone = done.contains("5A");

    // 31A (Section 10) is only needed for valid safeguarding institutions.
    // isValidSafeguardingInst() is the SAME rule handleResolutionCases uses
    // to decide whether 5A goes to 31A, so routing and this check match.
    // e.g. EMI only → not valid → Section 10 not needed → true.
    boolean section10Done = !isValidSafeguardingInst(merged) || done.contains("31A");

    LOGGER.info("[isGuidedPermissionJourneyComplete] 5A={} section10={} firmDataItemId={}",
            fiveADone, section10Done, firmDataItemId);

    return fiveADone && section10Done;
}
```

### Fix A: status read
**File:** `Rep027DbSyncService`, in `syncSpecialJourney`. Make this change in both places that read `existingStatus`.

```java
// WHY specialRowName AND NOT realSectionName:
//   During guided permission the DB row is still called "Special1" /
//   "Special2" / "Special3". The real name (e.g.
//   "SafeguardingReturn.SafeguardingInstInfo") has no row yet, so reading
//   by real name always returned null.
//
//   null made resolveResumePageId treat every save as a FIRST save and
//   return nextQidForStatus directly (e.g. 2A) WITHOUT checking whether
//   it was already answered. That page then forced the status to
//   IN PROGRESS even though the section was complete.
//
//   Reading by specialRowName returns the real status, so
//   resolveResumePageId walks the remaining questions and skips the
//   ones already answered.
String existingStatus = firmDataItemExtDao.getCompletionStatusForSection(
        firmDataItemId,
        REPConstants.SafeGuardingTaskGroup,
        specialRowName);   // was: realSectionName
```

### Fix B1: delete Special3
**File:** `DatabasePruningService`, in `deleteSections`. Add this after `dbSectionNames` is built and before the empty check.

```java
// WHY WE ALSO DELETE "Special3":
//   Rows are deleted by their real section name. But while guided
//   permission is still in progress, the Section 10 row is named
//   "Special3", not "SafeguardingReturn.SafeguardingUnrelatedPaymentServices".
//   So when Section 10 becomes hidden (e.g. 1A changed to EMI only),
//   the Special3 row never matched and was left behind in the DB.
//
//   We only add it when Section 10 is already being deleted, so other
//   sections are not affected. If no Special3 row exists (normal task
//   list flow), the delete simply matches 0 rows.
if (dbSectionNames.contains("SafeguardingReturn.SafeguardingUnrelatedPaymentServices")) {
    dbSectionNames.add(REPConstants.SPECIAL3);
    LOGGER.info("Section 10 hidden → also deleting guided permission row '{}' "
            + "for firmDataItemId: {}", REPConstants.SPECIAL3, firmDataItemId);
}
```

If `REPConstants` isn't imported in `DatabasePruningService` yet, add the import, or use the string `"Special3"` directly.

